Subject: gfx_pc: both eyes per host frame, and the per-eye projection fold

The visionOS 3D stereo mode's engine half (Phase 6 M3/dev1, D-049/D-050/D-055;
docs/visionos-3d-plan.md §2.3 and §2.4). Three changes, all behind
TARGET_OS_VISION:

  * gfx_run's body becomes gfx_run_eye, and gfx_run walks the display list
    TWICE per host frame at the SAME game time - eye L then eye R - into the
    two eye framebuffers of one ring slot. Slot 0 of the backend's framebuffer
    table already follows the current eye (patch 0031), so the MSAA resolve,
    copy_framebuffer, the Vivid Colours / Black Level grade pass and the
    readback all land on the eye being drawn with nothing else changed.

  * the signed per-eye view offset and the convergence skew are folded into
    the projection at the TWO sites that form MP - gfx_sp_matrix's tail and
    gfx_sp_pop_matrix - and never into rsp.P_matrix itself. A rewritten P
    would compound on the next G_MTX_MUL that arrives with G_MTX_PROJECTION,
    which is the doubled-offset bug sm64coopdx's D-026 paid for.

  * WHICH RULE a projection gets is read from a TAG the engine emits into the
    display list (patch 0032, src/include/gbiex.h), not recovered from the
    shape of the matrix. That is D-055, and it replaces D-049's three-class
    P-shape test, which was measured wrong on device: with 4J's XBLA release on
    it classified as much geometry "sky" as "world" (2290014 against 2266415),
    because PD's lists MULTIPLY into the projection and the product stops being
    axis-aligned. Half the room then had no eye offset at all, which is what
    the user saw as floating bodies, wrong doors and "trippy" ramps.

    Four rules now: WORLD (the full fold, and every untagged projection in the
    engine), SKY (the convergence skew only - a translation folded behind the
    camera rotation would be a world-space shift), GUN (the viewmodel converges
    at its own |mv[3][2]| with a separation scaled to that depth - D-049's
    C_gun = znear = 1.5 was a ~2.7 NDC-unit sideways shift, which is why the
    gun class counter read 247990 while the user could see no gun), and FLAT (no
    fold: bit-identical in both eyes, ON the panel - menuRender's own span, and
    an orthographic projection, of which this engine has a dozen contrary to
    §2.4).

2D is untouched and needs to be: PD's rectangles are computed straight in NDC
and never go through MP, so they are identical in both eyes - zero disparity
for the HUD, for free.

Everywhere else PD_VISION_STEREO is 0: PD_MP_UPDATE expands to the identical
gfx_matrix_mul call the code had before, the tag reader and the class state
disappear with it, the pre-swap capture's guard disappears, and gfx_run is
gfx_run_eye plus one tail call. The oracle's byte-for-byte replay parity is the
proof and the gate runs it.

